% p15: the case-analysis eliminator, USED. `Bool : Sort 0` with two constructors;
% `elim Bool_cases Bool 0` declares
%   Bool_cases : Pi (P : Bool -> Sort 0). P true -> P false -> Pi (x : Bool). P x.
% Applied to a motive P (an AXIOM, so no beta is needed -- k_conv is structural), the
% branches t f and the scrutinee `true`, it must have type `P true`: four dependent
% applications, three of them substituting into a codomain the kernel built itself.
% Also the first fixture to name a constructor: `const true` was 21 in the kernel
% before 2026-09-13 (kp_ctor parsed the name and dropped it) while the twin accepted.
1 sort 0
2 const Bool
3 const Bool
inductive Bool : 1 | true : 2 | false : 3
elim Bool_cases Bool 0
4 const Bool
5 sort 0
6 pi 4 5
axiom P : 6
7 const P
8 const true
9 app 7 8
axiom t : 9
10 const P
11 const false
12 app 10 11
axiom f : 12
13 const Bool_cases
14 const P
15 app 13 14
16 const t
17 app 15 16
18 const f
19 app 17 18
20 const true
21 app 19 20
22 const P
23 const true
24 app 22 23
check 21 : 24
